<div class="mb-4">
  <h2 style="font-weight: 700; color: #0F2A4A;">Order Retention Settings</h2>
  <p class="text-muted mb-0">
    Configure how long completed or cancelled orders are kept before being automatically removed from the database.
    Active orders (Pending, Processing, Shipped) are never affected.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="card-box" style="max-width: 700px;">
  <form action="/admin/order-retention" method="POST">
    <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center mb-4 pb-3" style="border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">
      <h5 class="m-0"><i class="fas fa-clock-rotate-left me-2"></i>Order Retention</h5>
      <div class="form-check form-switch">
        <input type="checkbox" class="form-check-input" id="autoDeleteSwitch" name="autoDelete"
               <%= settings.autoDelete ? 'checked' : '' %>>
        <label class="form-check-label" for="autoDeleteSwitch">Auto-delete expired orders</label>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mb-4">
      <label class="form-label fw-bold" for="retentionMonths">Retention Period</label>
      <select name="retentionMonths" id="retentionMonths" class="form-select" style="max-width: 240px;">
        <% allowedMonths.forEach(function(m) { %>
          <option value="<%= m %>" <%= settings.retentionMonths === m ? 'selected' : '' %>>
            <%= m %> month<%= m !== 1 ? 's' : '' %>
          </option>
        <% }) %>
      </select>
      <small class="text-muted d-block mt-1">
        Terminal orders (Delivered or Cancelled) will be removed this many months after reaching that status.
      </small>
    </div>

    <div class="alert alert-info py-2 px-3 small mb-4">
      <i class="fas fa-info-circle me-1"></i>
      <strong>How it works:</strong> When an order is marked as <em>Delivered</em> or <em>Cancelled</em>,
      an expiry date is calculated (<em>terminal date + retention period</em>). MongoDB automatically removes
      the order once that date is reached (within ~60 seconds of expiry).
      Orders that were Pending, Processing, or Shipped — and all orders created before this feature was enabled —
      are never automatically deleted.
    </div>

    <div class="alert alert-warning py-2 px-3 small mb-4">
      <i class="fas fa-triangle-exclamation me-1"></i>
      <strong>Changing the retention period</strong> will immediately recalculate the expiry date for all
      existing terminal orders that are already enrolled in retention. Orders with no expiry date set
      (created before retention was enabled) are not affected.
    </div>

    <div class="mt-4 text-end">
      <button type="submit" class="btn btn-admin-primary">
        <i class="fas fa-save me-1"></i> Save Settings
      </button>
    </div>

  </form>
</div>
